* PDF Viewing and Editing
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-07-08 Wed 11:41
:ARCHIVE_FILE: ~/.jdotfiles/doom.d/config.org
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: config
:END:

Keys:

 - C-j / C-k - Scroll up/down a page

TODO: I'm not sure if I like using emacs as a pdf viewer, so I might just remove this.
TODO: Can I select something and have it annotate a specific sentence/paragraph?   org-noter-insert-note just marks the page number.

#+BEGIN_SRC elisp
(after! pdf-view
  ;; open pdfs scaled to fit page
  (setq-default pdf-view-display-size 'fit-width)
  ;; automatically annotate highlights
  (setq pdf-annot-activate-created-annotations t
        org-noter-insert-note-no-questions t
        pdf-view-resize-factor 1.1)
  ;; faster motion
  (map!
   :map pdf-view-mode-map
   :n "g g"          #'pdf-view-first-page
   :n "G"            #'pdf-view-last-page
   :localleader
   (:desc "Insert" "i" 'org-noter-insert-note)
   ))
#+END_SRC

* org-rifle and org-ql
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-07-08 Wed 10:27
:ARCHIVE_FILE: ~/.jdotfiles/doom.d/config.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Org Mode
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: config
:END:

Removed during the 2026-07 modernization (ivy/company -> vertico/corfu).
=helm-org-rifle= drags in all of helm; =org-ql-find= gives the same "search all agenda
files, preview the content" behaviour without the helm dependency.  =SPC j r= now calls
a wrapper around =org-ql-find= over =org-agenda-files=.

Original note: helm-org-rifle also brings in helm whereas the rest of this config used
ivy, which caused things like org-capture to automatically try to use helm instead of
ivy.  org-rifle also showed some of the content while searching, which was nice for
telling apart notes with the same title/heading.

#+BEGIN_SRC emacs-lisp :tangle no
(package! helm-org-rifle)

(use-package! helm-org-rifle
  :defer t)
(map! :leader
      (:prefix ("j" . "justyn")
               (:desc "helm-org-rifle" "r" #'helm-org-rifle)))
#+END_SRC

* Company Completion
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-07-08 Wed 10:27
:ARCHIVE_FILE: ~/.jdotfiles/doom.d/config.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Editing
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: config
:END:

Replaced by corfu.  The corfu equivalents live in config.org (=corfu-auto=,
=corfu-auto-delay=, =corfu-auto-prefix=).  The corfu module already aborts completion
when leaving evil insert state, so the old =evil-normal-state-entry-hook= /
=company-abort= hook is no longer needed.  =company-show-numbers= has no direct corfu
equivalent (use =corfu-indexed-mode= or =corfu-quick= if wanted).

#+BEGIN_SRC emacs-lisp :tangle no
(after! company
  (setq company-idle-delay 0.5
        company-minimum-prefix-length 2)
  (setq company-show-numbers t)
  (add-hook 'evil-normal-state-entry-hook #'company-abort)) ;; make aborting less annoying.
#+END_SRC

* beancount -- vendored local-repo recipe
:PROPERTIES:
:ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-07-08 Wed 10:27
:ARCHIVE_FILE: ~/.jdotfiles/doom.d/config.org
:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Packages/beancount
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: config
:END:

Replaced by the official =:lang beancount= module (enabled in init.el), so the manually
vendored copy in =ext/beancount/= and this local-repo recipe are no longer needed.  The
beancount section in config.org now just adds the =outline-minor-mode= hook.

#+BEGIN_SRC emacs-lisp :tangle no
(package! beancount
  :recipe (:local-repo "ext/beancount"))
#+END_SRC

